# Workspace-level environment for the PUBLIC frontend repo.
#
# Copy to `.env` if you need any of it. Nothing here is a secret, and nothing
# here should ever become one.
#
# WHERE THE REST LIVES
#   Frontend .......... apps/web/.env.example  (NEXT_PUBLIC_AILX_API_BASE, the
#                       Clerk PUBLISHABLE key, base path, public origin)
#   Demo model proxy .. services/openrouter-proxy  (AILX_ALLOWED_ORIGINS)
#   Exam service ...... the PRIVATE ailx-backend repo. The database URL, the
#                       item-bank path, CLERK_SECRET_KEY, the OpenRouter key
#                       sealing secret and every reviewer allowlist live there.
#
# DO NOT PUT A SECRET IN THIS TREE. This repo is public, it has no API routes
# and no database client, and `packages/core/test/frontendOnly.test.ts` fails a
# build that adds one. If you came from the admin repo, do not copy its example
# across: an admin DATABASE_URL or an operational bank path does not belong
# here, in a .env, or in a comment.

# Cap the vitest worker pool. Memory sets the ceiling, not CPU. Default 4.
# AILX_TEST_FORKS=8

# Playwright only: the exam service the e2e suite drives. No default on
# purpose, and NEVER staging — every spec appends rows. Point it at a
# throw-away `services/api` from the private repo.
# AILX_E2E_API_BASE=http://localhost:8787

# Playwright only: which frontend the suite drives, and reusing a server that
# is already on the port. Reuse is opt-in because then YOU own what is there.
# AILX_E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3210
# AILX_E2E_PORT=3210
# AILX_E2E_REUSE_SERVER=1

# Skip the lefthook hooks for one command, e.g. `LEFTHOOK=0 git push` on a
# draft branch.
# LEFTHOOK=0
